Description: Fix GCC 15 libstdc++ std::optional::emplace() compatibility
 GCC 15's libstdc++ std::optional::emplace() requires is_constructible_v<T>
 to be satisfied. Structs with default member initializers are aggregates
 in C++20 but GCC 15's optional implementation doesn't handle this properly.
 Instead of using emplace(), use aggregate initialization with assignment.
 .
 Error was: no matching member function for call to 'emplace'
 candidate template ignored: requirement 'is_constructible_v<...>' was not
 satisfied
Author: Juan Manuel Mendez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-11-29

